+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "6a00d8cd",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "# 02 · Pronóstico y backtest rolling-origin (PLAN §3)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Cuatro modelos (Logit-ETS, Logit-ETS damped, factor de reparto, naive estacional), validados con *expanding window*: cada mes objetivo se entrena **solo** con datos anteriores. Requiere `data/raw/`."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "5037010d",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import sys\n",
+    "from pathlib import Path\n",
+    "ROOT = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
+    "if ROOT.name == \"notebooks\":\n",
+    "    ROOT = ROOT.parent\n",
+    "sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n",
+    "\n",
+    "import numpy as np\n",
+    "import pandas as pd\n",
+    "from src.etl.load import load_migration, load_occupancy, load_survey\n",
+    "from src.etl.clean import clean_migration, clean_occupancy, clean_survey\n",
+    "from src.config import SURVEY_BORDER_MAP, IZABAL_BORDERS\n",
+    "\n",
+    "pd.set_option(\"display.width\", 140)\n",
+    "from src.config import ISABAL_FEEDER_BORDERS, VISITOR_TYPES\n",
+    "from src.etl import transform as t\n",
+    "from src.models import forecast as fc"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "38e05237",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "occ_df = t.occupancy_series(clean_occupancy(load_occupancy()))\n",
+    "sur = clean_survey(load_survey())\n",
+    "mig = clean_migration(load_migration())\n",
+    "\n",
+    "occ = fc.como_serie(occ_df, \"indice_ocupacion\")\n",
+    "enc = fc.serie_mensual_encuesta(t.survey_izabal_daily(sur))\n",
+    "feeders = ISABAL_FEEDER_BORDERS or sorted(SURVEY_BORDER_MAP.values())\n",
+    "migra = fc.serie_mensual_migracion(t.migration_monthly(mig), feeders, VISITOR_TYPES)\n",
+    "print(\"ocupación:\", occ.index.min().date(), \"→\", occ.index.max().date(), \"· encuesta:\", enc.index.min().date(), \"→\", enc.index.max().date(), \"· NaN:\", int(enc.isna().sum()))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "5bcd970e",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## A. Ocupación de Izabal (acotada a [0, 1] → logit)\n",
+    "Historia mínima de ETS: 25 meses ⇒ con 36 meses quedan 11 folds (feb–dic 2025)."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "f83a2c7a",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "bt_occ = fc.backtest(occ, transform=\"logit\", bounds=(0, 1), migracion=migra)\n",
+    "met_occ = fc.metricas_backtest(bt_occ)\n",
+    "display(met_occ.round(4))\n",
+    "assert bt_occ[\"y_pred\"].dropna().between(0, 1).all()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "e2ef4323",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import plotly.graph_objects as go\n",
+    "fig = go.Figure()\n",
+    "fig.add_scatter(x=occ.index, y=occ.values, name=\"Observado\", line=dict(color=\"#0E7C86\"))\n",
+    "for m, dash in zip([\"logit_ets\", \"naive_estacional\"], [\"dash\", \"dot\"]):\n",
+    "    d = bt_occ[(bt_occ.modelo == m) & bt_occ.valido]\n",
+    "    fig.add_scatter(x=d.fecha, y=d.y_pred, name=fc.ETIQUETAS[m], mode=\"lines+markers\", line=dict(dash=dash, color=\"#7D3C98\" if m == \"logit_ets\" else \"#6C757D\"), marker=dict(symbol=\"circle-open\"))\n",
+    "fig.update_layout(title=\"Backtest rolling-origin · ocupación Izabal\", yaxis_range=[0, 1.05])\n",
+    "fig.show()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "cbdb99ce",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Pronóstico 2026 (Estimación)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "012d931c",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "fut = pd.concat([fc.pronostico(occ, 12, m, bounds=(0, 1), migracion=migra) for m in fc.MODELOS]).dropna(subset=[\"estimacion\"])\n",
+    "display(fut.pivot(index=\"fecha\", columns=\"modelo\", values=\"estimacion\").round(3))\n",
+    "assert fut[\"estimacion\"].between(0, 1).all()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "c725ba27",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## B. Encuesta: mes sin filas (2025-01) y backtest\n",
+    "⚠️ Con 6–117 registros/mes la serie es ruidosa: se reporta el error real. La transformación usada es `log1p` (conteos ≥ 0); el plan no la fija para la encuesta."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "50e8d789",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "bt_enc = fc.backtest(enc, transform=\"log\", bounds=(0, np.inf), migracion=migra, desde=\"2024-01-01\")\n",
+    "display(fc.metricas_backtest(bt_enc).round(3))\n",
+    "for m in fc.MODELOS:\n",
+    "    print(m, round(fc.imputar_mes(enc, \"2025-01-01\", m, transform=\"log\", bounds=(0, np.inf), migracion=migra), 1))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "9514f975",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## C. Pseudo-out-of-sample: ene–feb 2026 de la encuesta\n",
+    "Se enmascaran, se imputan con datos < t y se comparan contra el valor real."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "1e4807b7",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "filas = []\n",
+    "for f in [\"2026-01-01\", \"2026-02-01\"]:\n",
+    "    real = enc.get(pd.Timestamp(f), np.nan)\n",
+    "    for m in fc.MODELOS:\n",
+    "        est = fc.imputar_mes(enc.drop(index=[i for i in enc.index if i >= pd.Timestamp(f)]), f, m, transform=\"log\", bounds=(0, np.inf), migracion=migra)\n",
+    "        filas.append({\"fecha\": f, \"modelo\": m, \"real\": real, \"estimacion\": est, \"error_%\": 100 * abs(real - est) / real if real else np.nan})\n",
